---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Sancta Via — the apps" description="The Sancta Via family of Catholic companion apps: saints, devotions, novenas, prayer, confession, the liturgical calendar, and daily Scripture.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-24 pt-4">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl text-balance">Sancta Via — the apps</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none">
      <p>Seven companion apps for Catholic life, one design language: the
      cross, the path, and whatever the day or season asks of you. Every
      app works completely offline — your prayers don't need a signal.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4">
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Saints SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">The who's-who of heaven: 2,000+ saints with patronages, feast days, short bios, and — for hundreds of them — grounded, source-pinned life stories.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Devotions SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">Daily devotions and the season's practice: a routine that follows the liturgical year, morning and night.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Novena SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">Nine-day prayers with a candle that remembers where you left off.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Prayer SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">A pocket prayer book: classic prayers for every occasion, offline.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Confession SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">An examination of conscience and a step-by-step walk through the sacrament — private by design.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Calendar SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">The liturgical year in your pocket: today's feast, color, and season.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Bible Reader SV</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">Daily Scripture with a reading plan that fits the liturgical rhythm.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-xl text-brand">Support the work</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink">The apps are free, offline, and contain no advertising. If they've helped your prayer life, a small donation keeps the servers lit and the saints coming:</p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <!-- TODO: replace with your real link once the page exists. -->
        <a class="tap-target inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-full bg-brand px-4 text-sm text-white hover:opacity-90"
           href="https://buymeacoffee.com/REPLACE_ME" rel="noopener">Buy me a coffee</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">Privacy: the apps collect nothing, track nothing, and send nothing anywhere — <a href="/privacy/" class="text-brand hover:underline">read the one-paragraph policy</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
